From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matteo zappia <45754172+matteozappia@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:27:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] recovery: ask before installing an unverified package on a
 user build

A user build refused every package whose signature the recovery does not
trust, with no question. This product installs add-on packages (an
application suite, for example) that their own makers sign, so no key the
recovery carries verifies them. Ask the person at the screen on every build
type, as a debuggable build already does; a package that is not confirmed is
still refused, and one sideloaded with no text on the screen has nobody to
ask and is refused as before.
---
 recovery.cpp | 10 ++++------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/recovery.cpp b/recovery.cpp
index 44c7261f021c11bb3c02cd4e282879ae52662c97..07d2f3083a98ce18897b01d13ad3e61a2b118779 100644
--- a/recovery.cpp
+++ b/recovery.cpp
@@ -179,12 +179,10 @@ bool ask_to_ab_reboot(Device* device) {
 }
 
 bool ask_to_continue_unverified(Device* device) {
-  if (get_build_type() == "user") {
-    return false;
-  } else {
-    device->GetUI()->SetProgressType(RecoveryUI::EMPTY);
-    return yes_no(device, "Signature verification failed", "Install anyway?");
-  }
+  // The person at the screen decides, on a user build too: an add-on package is signed by its
+  // own maker, whose key no recovery trusts.
+  device->GetUI()->SetProgressType(RecoveryUI::EMPTY);
+  return yes_no(device, "Signature verification failed", "Install anyway?");
 }
 
 bool ask_to_continue_downgrade(Device* device) {
